        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, thank you for referring your 80-year-old male patient, admitted on 18/05/2021 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Physical examination confirmed bilateral expiratory wheeze. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Blood tests demonstrated mild systemic inflammation. The patient was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Oxygen saturation was monitored continuously via pulse oximetry. The patient responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. Discharge education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided. We recommend continued follow-up and optimisation of his inhaled maintenance therapy. Please do not hesitate to contact us if required. Kind regards, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>"
            },
